claim('CYCLE-RESIDUAL-IDENTITY','Endpoint differences telescope to zero on a declared directed closed walk, hence C(h-df)=C(h). For the rational triangle, df=(1/3,1/3,-2/3) and residual=(0,0,1); a constant potential shift changes neither. A zero sum suffices for a potential on the single cycle by successive partial sums.',[('_lev_examiner_theoretical_minimum_quiz/study_guide.md',[[21,51]]),('code/tests/test_007_worked_triangle.py',[[25,70]])],'Algebraic derivation under explicit orientation/coefficients; finite tests instantiate it. No quotient optimum, physical interpretation, learner gain or arbitrary-graph sufficiency inferred.')
claim('FAULT-SENSITIVE-CONTROL','A reversed difference convention also telescopes to zero and preserves the residual sum, so aggregate cycle-sum assertions accept this wrong-sign mutant. Independently computed coordinate checks distinguish it; equality of LP objectives similarly needs feasibility before serving as a certificate.',[('code/tests/test_007_evidence_boundaries.py',[[14,31]]),('_lev_examiner_theoretical_minimum_quiz/study_guide.md',[[55,63]])],'Demonstrates specific finite checker weaknesses, not complete adversarial robustness or sufficiency of all existing checkers.')
